# Hanging scenery vine, native 8x40, one frame: a thin pale olive stem with a few leaves, anchored at the top.
# Cosmetic: the runtime rotates it about the top centre when a falling stone lands (HangingVine). Not trap-vine (no thorn ball).
# Decor tier (D76, #344): pale dull olive, contour in its own hue, no ink 0b0814, no violet leaves; quiet against the level background (D92).
# Night palette (D92, #430): every colour mixed 35 % toward the night background 2c3f66; the day values are in docs/ART_DIRECTION.md.
# Layered-forest recolour (#236, D112): OKLab L x0.6, in front of the canopy clump the vines hang from (terrain.grid `canopy-*`):
# outline 0.120, body 0.139.
# Floor raise (#648): the trees behind the vines rose 16 px, so every colour is x1.1 to keep the D76 decor body over 0.08
# (0.084 to 0.180 over every placement, from 0.079 before the lift).
size 8 40
# Depth palette (D120, 2026-11-21): the same lightness per key in moss green (hue 136, C 0.03), contour k bark.
color k 3a2f26
color n 384333
color N 323e2c
color l 384332
color d 2f3a2a
frame hang
